"D4"},{"name":"Mustafa Abdel Aziz","role":"Drone [Arghul]","tracks":"D4"},{"name":"Bill Cobham","role":"Drums, Tambourine","tracks":"D4"},{"name":"David Rhodes","role":"Guitar [Steinberger]","tracks":"D4"},{"name":"David Sancious","role":"Organ [Hammond]","tracks":"D4"},{"name":"Peter Gabriel","role":"Synthesizer [Prophet 5, Roland D-50], Voice, Percussion [Additional], Piano, Drums [Doholla]","tracks":"D4"},{"name":"David Bottrill","role":"Tambourine [2], Performer [Distorted Slide]","tracks":"D4"},{"name":"Shankar","role":"Electric Violin [Double Violin]","tracks":"D5"},{"name":"David Rhodes","role":"Guitar [Ebow]","tracks":"D5"},{"name":"Peter Gabriel","role":"Synthesizer [Prophet 5], Voice, Contrabass","tracks":"D5"},{"name":"Richard Evans","role":"Tin Whistle","tracks":"D5"}],"notes":"Direct Metal Mastering\n\nMusic for The Last Temptation Of Christ, a film by Martin Scorsese.\n\nRecorded between February 1988 and March 1989 at Real World Studios, Box, England. Mastered at Precision Lacquer.\n\n\"I have put together two albums around the music  of The Last Temptation of Christ. This album is my work; the other, Passion Sources, represents a selection of some of the traditional music, sources of inspiration and location recordings. I was excited to be asked to work on the music. When I first discussed the project with Martin  Scorsese in 1983 I wanted to find out how he was intending to film this controversial novel. He wanted to present the struggle between the humanity and the divinity of Christ in a powerful and original way, and I was convinced by his commitment to the spiritual content and message. He is an excellent and very musical director and working with him has been a great experience.\nAfter we finished mixing the film there were some unfinished ideas that needed developing and I took some extra time to complete this record. There are several pieces that were not able to be included in the film and I felt that the record should be able to stand as a separate body of work. I chose the working title for the film - Passion.\nWe recorded some of the finest singers and soloists in the field of world music and we set the score on a backdrop of traditional North African rhythms and sounds. It was a wonderful experience working with such different and idiosyncratic musicians. They came from Pakistan, Turkey, India, Ivory Coast, Bahrain, Egypt, New Guinea, Morocco, Senegal and Ghana. For many of them working with this material was something quite new and they were very enthusiastic. The soundtrack is full of the spirit of their performances.\" Peter Gabriel\n\nThe following tracks contain selections from existing recordings of traditional music.\nTrack A1 - The Doudouks are playing an Armenian melody 'The Wind Subsides', recorded for Ocora Records under the direction of Robert Ataian.\nTrack A4 - Incorporates a traditional melody from Kurdistan. Kurdish Duduks are from Unesco Collection - A Musical Anthology of the Orient, General Editor Alain Danielou for Musicaphon Records.\nTrack B1 - Written around a traditional Egyptian rhythm which is performed to fend off evil spirits.\nTrack B3 - Based on an improvisation by Shankar and Peter Gabriel.\nTrack B4 - The Ney Flute is playing a traditional Armenian melody.\nTrack C2 - Based on an improvisation by Mahmoud and Peter Gabriel.\n\nGeffen Records, Manufactured exclusively by Warner Bros. records, Inc., A Warner Communications Company.\n© 1989 Realworld/Virgin Records Ltd.\n℗ 1989 The David Geffen Company.\nMade in U.S.A.\n\nAll compositions by Peter Gabriel and published by Peter Gabriel Limited PRS, adm. by Hidden Pun Music, Inc. BMI.\nB3 also published by Ganesh Music, adm. by Warner-Tamerlane Publishing Corp. BMI.\nC2 also \"published\" by Copyright Control, adm. by Hidden Pun Music, Inc. BMI.\n\nBlack & white printed inner sleeves with credits and pictures.\n\nOriginally issued with a large hype sticker on the shrinkwrap. Promotional copies will have the sticker directly placed on the cover because they were not shinkwrapped.","images":[{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/u1uWV6ng-BcThlZrM0jxXu6nk2wY3BJYD-WoeBTjSYk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:596/w:599/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDI1/MC5qcGVn.jpeg","width":599,"height":596,"type":"primary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/H93MeTdDtU53aAXgckB48oY3bTVRT3O39rrxHtAUQ7A/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:595/w:599/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDI2/MC5qcGVn.jpeg","width":599,"height":595,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/dL_wdBz8LelchwJYoF-0tJ7lxmGl3WJG64qLSa_erNw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:578/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDI4/Mi5qcGVn.jpeg","width":578,"height":600,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/FloObPoeKl9ismkd9VUqDuUAhBPNLkyBgu0RbV8GLI4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:576/w:599/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDI5/MC5qcGVn.jpeg","width":599,"height":576,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/KoNCKvTrUyzNP-TDPtmUN8QE3Aee4jMtPfg78fQXJ00/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:580/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDMy/MC5qcGVn.jpeg","width":580,"height":600,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/NuF7GnlLdT5GWbR2u5KJI4dv14EENH1OlK16TOZHMCo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:589/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDMz/MC5qcGVn.jpeg","width":589,"height":600,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/visNlFvm7l4N1GgXleJCRCnR_9b2KXJ0x6cMd6TvUGU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:591/w:599/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDI2/Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","width":599,"height":591,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/E-qBI9MU4dctJyXeje9Ai6ATeUGo4gTPwBq6cRe7rj0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:589/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9SLTIxOTQ3/NzEtMTI2OTEzNDI3/NC5qcGVn.jpeg","width":600,"height":589,"type":"secondary"},{"uri":"https://i.discogs.com/D-KJvPuAAe9SUwaG_cV1zdT9XyzXel3PQmxG8AqBVnI/rs:fit/g:s